WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:15,660
MCP or modified citrus pectin is referenced in your cancer book as an important supplement to take

00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:23,420
to help prevent metastasis. I've already had my lung cancer metastasis once. Would this be a good

00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:31,740
addition for my supplement protocol? Well, modified citrus pectin would not be contraindicated for anybody.

00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:41,260
So yes, you could add modified citrus pectin to your protocol. Now, a couple downsides with modified

00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:47,340
citrus pectin. We have some people that are taking it and are putting it right in their smoothie

00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:54,220
with the other things that they have in their smoothie, whatever it is and blending it and

00:00:54,220 --> 00:01:01,420
drinking it that way. That seems to work well. If you're going to take modified citrus pectin

00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:09,420
the powder and you're going to take it separate from a smoothie, the water it is, it doesn't dissolve

00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:16,940
in water really at all and you're going to get frustrated. It does dissolve instantly in a little

00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:22,860
orange juice. Orange juice is a lot of sugar. Yeah, but if you just do three ounces of orange juice,

00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:29,180
put your modified citrus pectin. It'll dissolve and make it thicker, but then you'll be able to

00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:37,020
go up that down if you're not taking it with a smoothie. It's best to put it in orange juice. I know

00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:43,340
some people have put it with some lemon juice or some lemonade. It has to be like a citrus juice

00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:51,340
in order for it to absorb well. If you read the literature, the literature that I've read

00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:58,620
written about modified citrus pectin in a perfect scenario, you're taking it more on an empty stomach

00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:08,700
with some orange juice, but we also realize that it's really hard to live in a perfect scenario. I

00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:14,700
talk to people all the time that are like, it's really hard for me to split my supplements up

00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:23,980
three times a day. Life gets in the way, so it's difficult to stay on a protocol where you're taking

00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:29,980
that on a relatively empty stomach and you've got so many other different pieces of your protocol. It's

00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:36,060
hard to stay motivated, especially if you're doing well to stick to something like that. So I've

00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:40,060
always told people just go ahead and it's easier. Just put it in your smoothie. It's just going to be

00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:47,180
easier to do it. Still going to get 99% of the benefit of it. But is there anything wrong with somebody

00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:53,340
adding modified citrus pectin that I didn't tell them to add? No, everybody can add that there's no

00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:54,940
down side to that.

